dvasser@yahoo.com (The Oracle  DBA) writes:
> But, now that I'm at experience level 30 I have a question.  Can a
> *cubus give me MORE experience points so that I can further advance
> some skills that have an * marked next to them?  I danced with a
> *cubus and even though it said "That was a very educational
> experience" I saw that I didn't receive any experience points for the
> encounter.  How do I get them to give me more XP?

*cubi don't give you experience points directly (except by killing
them); they raise you to the next level, and your experience points
are set to the threshold required for that level. Since there is no
"next level" from 30, "educational experiences" will have no effect
other than the wisdom exercise.

> By the way, I have an * next to enchantment spells.  When I go to
> enhance my skills yhe line at the top says (Skills flagged by a "*"
> may be enhanced if skill slots become available).  Will a *cubus give
> me more experience for skill slots so I can advance my enchantment
> spells farther along?  Or am I out of skill slots now that I'm at XP
> level 30?  Is there a limit?

There is a limit, and you're at it. The only way to advance skills
further would be to get yourself leveldrained below 30 (automatically
unenhancing skills that no longer fit into the available slots, last
in first out) and assign your slots differently when you regain the
levels.

